: But say in a word, (alla eipe logw, speak to thy word,) and my servant shall be healed."  This is the sum of what this very able commentator says on the subject. 

In Dr. Dodd's collections we find the following:- 

"The word of God, which promises to the faithful, an entrance into God's rest in David's time, and now to us, is not a thing which died or was forgotten as soon as it was uttered, but it continues one and the same to all generations; it is zwn, quick or living.  So Isaiah says: The word of our God shall stand for ever;
